---
import AeroStudyMeta from '../../../components/AeroStudyMeta.astro';
const endpoint=import.meta.env.PUBLIC_AERO_CHAT_URL||'';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>Aero · Cooling-channel study</title><meta name="description" content="Compare three cooling-channel layouts against a thermal and pressure budget. Review the equations and download a reproducible LaTeX paper."/></head>
<body><main data-cooling data-endpoint={endpoint}>
<header><a href="/software/aero/" class="brand">AERO <small>Cooling-channel study</small></a><nav><a href="/software/aero/#capability-papers">Capability papers</a><a href="/software/aero/current/?study=channel">Flow study</a><button data-example>Load worked example</button></nav></header>
<AeroStudyMeta label="Aero analytical study" />
<nav class="stages" aria-label="Study stages">{['Requirements','Math','Layouts','Compare','Report'].map((name,i)=><button data-stage={i}><span>0{i+1}</span><b>{name}</b><small data-progress-label>Inputs needed</small><progress max="100" value="0"></progress></button>)}</nav>
<div class="workspace"><aside><div class="pane-heading"><small>ENGINEERING PARTNER</small><h1>Which layout keeps the wall cool?</h1><p data-model role="status">Checking model…</p></div><div class="conversation" data-conversation role="log" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="notice" data-missing role="status"></p><form data-chat><label for="question">Discuss the requirements</label><textarea id="question" rows="3" maxlength="4000" placeholder="What geometry do you need before we can compare layouts?"></textarea><button data-send>Ask Aero ↑</button></form><small class="scope">Live chat explains. Only your reviewed numeric inputs start a calculation. Chat cannot change them or run a solver.</small></aside>
<section class="work"><div class="pane-heading"><small>ANALYTICAL FIRST CUT · NOT THERMAL CFD</small><h2 data-heading>Define heat, flow and limits.</h2><p data-notice role="status">Start with your requirements or load the worked example.</p></div><div class="content">
<section data-part="0"><div class="inputs">{[['heat_w','Heat into coolant (W)',10,150,1,100],['flow_ml_s','Total water flow (mL/s)',.5,2,.1,1],['inlet_c','Inlet temperature (°C)',15,35,1,25],['wall_limit_c','Inner-wall limit (°C)',40,85,1,72],['pressure_budget_pa','Friction budget (Pa)',100,10000,100,2000],['length_mm','Heated length (mm)',300,800,10,''],['available_width_mm','Available array width (mm)',4,30,1,'']].map(([key,label,min,max,step,value])=><label>{label}<input type="number" data-input={key} min={min} max={max} step={step} value={value} required/></label>)}</div><details><summary>Model assumptions and what “wall” means</summary><p>Straight circular passages. Equal heat and flow sharing. Uniform heat flux around the entire wetted perimeter. Fixed water properties near 25 °C. No solid conduction, manifold losses, hot spots, phase change, or manufacturing CAD. The wall limit is the fluid-contact surface—not the outside of a component.</p><p>Layouts: 4 × 1 mm, 2 × 2 mm, 1 × 4 mm. The fixed 1 mm ligament is an assumed spacing, not a verified tolerance.</p></details><label class="confirm"><input type="checkbox" data-confirm/> I reviewed these inputs and the model assumptions.</label><button class="primary" data-prepare>Prepare comparison →</button></section>
<section data-part="1" hidden><p>The coolant rise follows the energy balance. Diameter and channel count determine wall-to-fluid resistance and pumping demand.</p><div data-math></div><details><summary>Adverse scenarios</summary><p>Thermal: heat +10%, flow −10%, heat-transfer coefficient −20%. Pressure: viscosity +20%, flow +10%, diameter −2%. These are separate scenario checks, not statistical uncertainty bounds.</p></details></section>
<section data-part="2" hidden><div class="layout-controls"><label>Inspect layout <select data-layout><option value="0">A · 4 × 1 mm</option><option value="1" selected>B · 2 × 2 mm</option><option value="2">C · 1 × 4 mm</option></select></label><span data-layout-size></span></div><div data-geometry class="geometry"></div><p class="scope">Parametric fluid passages. Drag to rotate; scroll to zoom. Diameter and spacing exaggerated ×15 for inspection. No imported CAD or CFD mesh is claimed.</p></section>
<section data-part="3" hidden><p>Compute three layouts, check energy closure and the radial heat-transfer reference, then compile the paper.</p><button class="primary" data-run>Start analytical study + PDF</button><p class="scope">Runs in the isolated report worker. No CFD solver is launched. Same shared limits as the flow study: two runs per visitor per hour. Evidence retained for 48 hours.</p></section>
<div class="job" data-job hidden><b data-job-label></b><progress max="3" value="0" data-job-progress></progress><p data-job-message></p></div>
<section data-part="4" hidden><h3 data-decision>No current result yet.</h3><div class="table-scroll" data-table></div><div data-result-chart></div><p data-checks></p><div class="downloads" data-downloads hidden><a data-pdf target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="primary">PDF paper ↗</a><a data-evidence>LaTeX + evidence ↓</a></div><details><summary>What remains before thermal CFD or a hardware decision?</summary><p>Manufactured geometry, heated footprint, wall material and thickness, contact resistance, real fluid properties, flow sharing, manifold and bend losses, absolute pressure, boiling/mixed-convection checks, and a matched experimental or independent thermal reference.</p></details><p class="scope">This is a reproducible analytical screen. It does not establish a safe hardware operating point or validated thermal CFD.</p></section>
</div><footer><button data-back>← Back</button><span data-step-note>Requirements before execution</span><button data-next>Math →</button></footer></section></div>
</main><script>import '../../../lib/aero/cooling-workspace';</script></body></html>
<style>
main{display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100dvh}header,.stages{flex-shrink:0}.workspace{flex:1;min-height:0!important;height:auto!important}aside{min-height:0}.conversation{min-height:0}progress{appearance:none;border:0;background:#2b414d}progress::-webkit-progress-bar{background:#2b414d}progress::-webkit-progress-value{background:#47b9e0}.stages button[data-done=true] progress::-webkit-progress-value{background:#5ac39a}.job progress::-webkit-progress-value{background:#e3bd53}.job[data-state=complete] progress::-webkit-progress-value{background:#5ac39a}.job[data-state=failed] progress::-webkit-progress-value{background:#ef7575}@media(max-width:760px){main{height:auto}.workspace{min-height:0!important}.conversation{min-height:100px}}
